  "scene_authority_rules": [
    "Resolve world positions from Node3D.GlobalTransform and child Marker3D",
    "Stable IDs are separate from world coordinates",
    "Use scene-authored NPC and traffic route markers, not catalogue coordinates",
    "Edit scenes/world/Town.tscn and scenes/world/assets directly; there is no bake step",
    "Never copy dynamic bridge/swing/furniture states into the authored town",
    "Playground interaction positions come from Playground/WorksiteMarker, never C# coordinates",
    "Gable ends belong on the ridge ends (GableEast/GableWest), not the eave walls",
    "Panel-mounted sign and banner text uses two fixed faces; floating status labels may billboard",
    "CelebrationDecor bunting must not cast shadows",
    "NPC nameplates and portraits use distance scaling and a bounded visibility range"
  ],
  "runtime_deviations": [
    "Town.tscn is the runtime copy of Town_Assets.tscn; it adds three SignSocket instances and a scene-owned RaceStart marker required by existing gameplay IDs.",
    "BakeryOrderSlot.tscn and ShelfBookSlot.tscn are authored slot scenes added under BakeryStall and LibraryShelf because the candidate scene did not expose those stable gameplay paths.",
    "Town-road collision is a flat y=0 roadbed while the visual slabs stay 2-3.4 cm proud, removing vertical lips at road junctions and the bridge deck without changing the authored road surfaces.",
    "The swing frame assets contain four BROKEN labels (two per frame), so restoration counts every scene-authored label rather than assuming two.",
    "No scooter GLB is supplied; the town_scooter route keeps its stable route ID and uses the green town-car visual template.",
    "The playground WorksiteMarker lives inside Playground.tscn; the PlaygroundCenter gameplay anchor is validated against the Playground root at load, and the interaction station uses the marker.",
    "CelebrationDecor is a compact free-standing banner at the M20 festival entrance, in front of the bunting line; it no longer overlaps the Town Hall frontage.",
    "The DirectionPost is an authored four-arm stack at (-5, 0, -4.5) on the south verge, clear of Milo, the Delivery Board and Market Stock.",
    "Building gables use StandardMaterial3D_Gable with disable_receive_shadows so roof overhangs cannot read as open pediments.",
    "The M17 MarketStock is at (9.2, 0, 3.8) in front of the market, clear of the M16 DeliveryBoard at (-2.5, 0, 4.2)."
  ],
  "migration_acceptance_test": "Move ClothesShop and its DoorMarker 5 m in Godot: interaction follows without editing C#; v1.2.1 saves still restore."
}
